    "## 5. Text Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "Text preprocessing prepares raw messages for machine learning by reducing unnecessary variations and removing selected unwanted text elements.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following operations are applied:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Lowercase conversion:** Converts uppercase letters into lowercase.\n",
    "2. **URL removal:** Removes web addresses.\n",
    "3. **Email address removal:** Removes email addresses when present.\n",
    "4. **Punctuation removal:** Removes punctuation symbols.\n",
    "5. **Number removal:** Removes numerical characters.\n",
    "6. **Stopword removal:** Removes selected common English words using NLTK.\n",
    "7. **Tokenization:** Splits the text into individual words.\n",
    "\n",
    "The cleaned messages are used for TF-IDF feature extraction.\n",
    "\n",
    "Preprocessing may remove useful information in some cases, so its effect on classification performance should be considered.\n"
   ]
  },
