    "## 9. Model Evaluation Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "The models are evaluated using the following metrics:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Accuracy\n",
    "\n",
    "The proportion of all messages correctly classified by the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Precision\n",
    "\n",
    "The proportion of messages predicted as spam that are actually spam.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Recall\n",
    "\n",
    "The proportion of actual spam messages correctly identified by the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "### F1-score\n",
    "\n",
    "The harmonic mean of precision and recall.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Confusion Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "A table showing correct and incorrect predictions for the ham and spam classes.\n",
    "\n",
    "These metrics provide a more complete assessment of classification performance than accuracy alone. Precision, recall, and F1-score are particularly useful when the dataset has unequal class distributions.\n"
   ]
