   "source": [
    "### Why Is Recall Important in Spam Detection?\n",
    "\n",
    "Recall is important because it measures the proportion of actual spam messages correctly identified by the model. A low recall means that many spam messages are incorrectly classified as legitimate messages and may reach the user's inbox.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example, if 100 messages are actually spam and the model detects only 80, its spam recall is 80%. The remaining 20 spam messages are false negatives.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, precision is also important because incorrectly classifying legitimate messages as spam can cause users to miss important communications. Therefore, a good spam detection system should aim for high recall while maintaining acceptable precision.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2da6e0fc-6139-44aa-9453-d4574990b800",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Importance of Recall in Spam Detection\n",
    "\n",
    "Recall is particularly important because it measures how many actual spam messages are correctly identified by the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "A false negative occurs when an actual spam message is classified as ham. Such a message may reach the user's inbox without being detected.\n",
    "\n",
    "For example, if a dataset contains 100 actual spam messages and a model correctly identifies 80 of them, the spam recall is 80%.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, maximizing recall alone is not sufficient. A model with low precision may incorrectly classify legitimate messages as spam. Therefore, spam detection should aim for high recall while maintaining acceptable precision.\n",
    "\n",
    "The appropriate balance depends on the intended use of the spam detection system.\n"
   ]
  },
